MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Ronettes and Lesley Gore feel like natural next choices because they combine the mid-'60s pop appeal of AM Gold with the artist hits collections I often choose.",
    "Otis Redding and Hall & Oates offer familiar songs in a best-of collection, matching my interest in older hits and pop-rock. Another Christmas collection also feels timely after A Very Special Christmas."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Star Trek soundtrack misses my current interest in songs by familiar performers; being an older recording does not make a film score appealing to me.",
    "The James Bond collection centers on a film series, while I am more interested in an artist's songs. Graceland appeals through my Simon & Garfunkel listening, but a single album is less tempting than a hits collection today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "An older release or nostalgic association alone seems to count too much; I care about the performers and songs, not just the era.",
    "The words 'best of' do not make every collection equally appealing: film themes interest me less than an artist's familiar hits."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My strongest preference today is for mid-'60s pop collections, which makes the Ronettes and Lesley Gore more compelling than other broadly suitable hits collections.",
    "I can like a recommendation without choosing it now: Elvis and Earth Wind & Fire fit my taste, but they are lower priorities than the '60s pop collections on this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in older hits collections, but sometimes stretch nostalgia too far and miss my stronger preference for mid-'60s pop today."
}
